    {
      "paper_id": "doi:10.1007/s10640-023-00770-w",
      "sequence": 3,
      "source_sequence": 385,
      "article_type": "research-article",
      "title_en": "Spatio-Temporal Analysis of Game Harvests in Sweden",
      "title_cn": "瑞典狩猎收获的时空分析",
      "authors": [
        "Julian E. Lozano",
        "Katarina Elofsson",
        "Yves Surry",
        "George Marbuah"
      ],
      "abstract_en": "The benefits and costs of wildlife are contingent on the spatial overlap of animal populations with economic and recreational human activities. By using a production function approach with dynamic spatial panel data models, we analyze the effects of human hunting and carnivore predation pressure on the value of ungulate game harvests. The results show evidence of dynamic spatial dependence in the harvests of roe deer and wild boar, but not in those of moose, which is likely explained by the presence of harvesting quotas for the latter. Results suggest the impact of lynx on roe deer harvesting values is reduced by 75% when spatial effects are taken into account. The spatial analysis confirms that policymakers’ aim to reduce wild boar populations through increased hunting has been successful, an effect that was only visible when considering spatial effects.",
      "abstract_cn": "野生动物的收益和成本取决于动物种群与经济及娱乐性人类活动的空间重叠。通过使用生产函数方法和动态空间面板数据模型，我们分析了人类狩猎和食肉动物捕食压力对有蹄类狩猎收获价值的影响。结果显示，狍和野猪的收获存在动态空间依赖性，但驼鹿则不然，这很可能由后者存在狩猎配额来解释。结果表明，当考虑空间效应时，猞猁对狍狩猎价值的影响减少了75%。空间分析证实，政策制定者通过增加狩猎来减少野猪种群的目标已经成功，这一效应仅在考虑空间效应时才显现。",
